These files are NOT covered by the MIT licence that covers the source code. The
name "transport-io" and the marks in this directory are excluded from that grant.

Copyright and trademark are separate things, and MIT speaks only to the first. It
grants rights to copy and modify a work. It does not grant permission to use a
project's name and mark to identify something else. This file removes that
ambiguity rather than leaving it to be argued about.

YOU MAY, without asking:

  Use the marks to refer to this project. Articles, talks, slides, comparison
  tables, "built with transport-io" badges, a dependency list, a conference
  sticker about the project.

  Reproduce them unaltered, at any size, in either the ink or bone colourway.

  Link to them.

YOU MAY NOT:

  Use them as the mark of your own project, product, or company, including a
  fork.

  Modify them: no recolouring, rotating, skewing, outlining, adding effects,
  reseating the wedge, or combining them with other marks.

  Use them in a way that implies this project endorses, sponsors, or is
  affiliated with you when it does not.

  Register them, or anything confusingly similar, as a trademark.

A fork is welcome and the code licence permits it. Ship it under your own name
and your own mark.

The wordmark in the lockup is set in IBM Plex Mono, which is licensed under the
SIL Open Font License by IBM and is not covered by this file or owned by this
project.

If you want to do something this file does not cover, ask. The answer is usually
yes.
